  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with a history of transient cerebral ischemic attacks and unspecified cardiac arrhythmia (diagnosis codes G45.9, I49.9), reporting intermittent episodes of dizziness and palpitations that are poorly correlated with standard ECG findings. To evaluate for paroxysmal atrial fibrillation or other intermittent dysrhythmias that may be contributing to these transient neurological symptoms, a cardiac event monitoring study (CPT 93271) is indicated. This service is medically necessary to identify the intermittent dysrhythmias underlying the patient's transient cerebral ischemic attacks."
